-Thank you!

535
00:27:39,300 --> 00:27:42,667
-而且你的上衣还挺透的……
-我知道，我刚才也才意识到。
-And your top's more
see through...
-I know, I just realised that.

536
00:27:42,700 --> 00:27:45,100
-你刚走出来我就注意到了。
-走光得有多厉害？
-I just noticed as you
walked out.
-How bad is it?

537
00:27:45,133 --> 00:27:46,633
-相当透。
-挺严重的。
-It's quite bad.
-It's quite bad.

538
00:27:46,667 --> 00:27:49,000
-别担心。
-我的文胸其实也是透视的。
呜呼！
-Don't worry.
-My bra's see-through, too.
Whoo hoo!

539
00:27:49,033 --> 00:27:50,933
-真的假的？
-假的，开玩笑的。
-Is it really?
-No that's a joke.

540
00:27:51,400 --> 00:27:53,733
才不是呢！（笑）
No! (LAUGHS)

541
00:27:53,967 --> 00:27:55,600
就是真的。
It is.

542
00:27:55,633 --> 00:27:59,067
不管怎样，听说你写自传，
Anyway, listen, is it true
that you wrote your
autobiography

543
00:27:59,100 --> 00:28:02,167
-是因为听说有人要给你出传记？
-对。
-because you heard
a biography was coming out?
-Yeah.

544
00:28:02,267 --> 00:28:04,267
-我听说有别人打算写我。
-嗯。
-I heard somebody else was
gonna write one.
-Yeah.

545
00:28:04,300 --> 00:28:06,867
我敢肯定
那里面绝对全是一堆屁话。
I was pretty convinced
it was gonna be
full of crap.

546
00:28:06,900 --> 00:28:08,567
-是啊。
-所以我就琢磨着
-Yeah.
-And so I thought

547
00:28:08,600 --> 00:28:11,700
不如我自己……呃，
亲自操刀写一本。
I'd have, um,
have a go myself.

548
00:28:11,733 --> 00:28:13,333
那本传记出版了吗？
还是被你……
Did it come out,
the biography?
Or did you...

549
00:28:13,367 --> 00:28:15,933
-出了，确实出了。
-真出了？
里面全是屁话吗？
-Yeah, no, it came out.
-It came out?
Was it full of crap?

550
00:28:15,967 --> 00:28:18,600
其实我都懒得看。
我盯了盯销量，
I didn't actually look at it.
I watched its sales,

551
00:28:18,633 --> 00:28:21,833
卖得并不怎么样。
不过话说回来，我自己的书也没好到哪去。
it didn't do so well.
But then nor did mine.

552
00:28:24,067 --> 00:28:25,533
哎，至少你那本是有真材实料的。
Well, it's not like
it wasn't full of stuff.

553
00:28:25,567 --> 00:28:27,533
总不像韦恩·鲁尼那本，
他出书那会儿才大概四岁——
It's not like Wayne Rooney's
because he was about four

554
00:28:27,567 --> 00:28:28,900
-就动笔写自传了。
-这倒是真的。
-when he wrote his.
-That is true.

555
00:28:28,933 --> 00:28:30,967
-你读过他的书吗？
-我脑子进水了才读那玩意儿。
-Have you read his?
-Of course I haven't read it.

556
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:32,167
也是。
Right.

557
00:28:32,200 --> 00:28:34,500
出生，长了对大耳朵，
踢足球，
Was born, grew big ears,
kicked football,

558
00:28:34,533 --> 00:28:35,567
跟老奶奶睡了一觉。
不好意思……
slept with grandmother.
Sorry...

559
00:28:35,600 --> 00:28:37,100
（观众大笑）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

560
00:28:38,300 --> 00:28:39,667
你的书肯定不至于像他那样，
It's not gonna be like yours,

561
00:28:39,700 --> 00:28:41,733
-咱们实话实说吧。
-别。
-let's be brutally honest.
-No.

562
00:28:41,767 --> 00:28:43,167
那你为什么不演
《神秘博士》了？
So why have you given up
Doctor Who?

563
00:28:43,200 --> 00:28:46,167
这也是我家八岁小孩
最想问的问题。
Which is the question most
asked by my eight-year-old.

564
00:28:46,200 --> 00:28:47,867
因为，呃……
Because, um,

565
00:28:47,900 --> 00:28:49,700
就觉得是时候离开了。
it just felt like the
right time to go.

566
00:28:49,733 --> 00:28:51,733
我在加的夫呆了整整两年。
I was two years in Cardiff.

567
00:28:51,767 --> 00:28:53,467
-噢，你……
-我知道！（笑）
-Oh. You...
-I know! (LAUGHS)

568
00:28:53,500 --> 00:28:55,100
（观众笑声）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

569
00:28:55,133 --> 00:28:56,733
我都没意识到！
I hadn't realised!

570
00:28:57,533 --> 00:28:59,133
天哪，我之前在那儿呆过两天！
God, I once went there
for two days!

571
00:28:59,167 --> 00:29:01,933
-我要遭天谴了！
-我还挺喜欢那儿的。
-I'm going to hell!
-I liked it very much.

572
00:29:01,967 --> 00:29:05,567
呃，没有啦，我就是想
尝试点别的新鲜事。
Um, no. I just wanted
to try some other stuff.

573
00:29:05,600 --> 00:29:08,100
好，在略过《神秘博士》的话题前，
Okay, now, just before we move
off Doctor Who,

574
00:29:08,133 --> 00:29:09,533
我还有一个重要问题。
I've got one
important question.

575
00:29:09,567 --> 00:29:11,367
戴立克的极速是多少？
What is the top speed
of a Dalek?

576
00:29:13,533 --> 00:29:15,700
我猜时速6英里？
I'm saying 6 miles per hour?

577
00:29:15,733 --> 00:29:17,267
-它们只能跑6英里？
-嗯。
-They only do 6?
-Hmm.

578
00:29:17,267 --> 00:29:20,067
-你跑得比戴立克还快？
-那是。
-You can run faster
than a Dalek?
-I can.

579
00:29:20,100 --> 00:29:21,700
那你干嘛还那么怕它们？
Why are you so
scared of them, then?

580
00:29:23,267 --> 00:29:24,700
它们看起来很有威胁嘛。
They're threatening things.

581
00:29:24,733 --> 00:29:25,967
-而且体型巨大！
-很大吗？
-They're huge!
-Are they huge?

582
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:27,433
它们跟你个头差不多大吧。
They're about the same
size as you.

583
00:29:27,467 --> 00:29:28,833
我单挑能干趴一个。
I could have one.

584
00:29:30,100 --> 00:29:31,733
呃，对了，是真的吗……
Um, now, Is it true...

585
00:29:31,767 --> 00:29:33,267
显然我们得先给不知情的观众
普及一下背景。
Obviously we have to get it
across for those
who don't know.

586
00:29:33,267 --> 00:29:35,700
-你曾嫁给克里斯·埃文斯。
-对。
-You know, you were married
to Chris Evans.
-Yeah.

587
00:29:35,733 --> 00:29:38,133
听说他当年是用一辆法拉利来泡你的，
是真的吗？
Is it true he tried to
pull you with a Ferrari?

588
00:29:38,167 --> 00:29:39,767
是真的。
That is true.

589
00:29:39,800 --> 00:29:41,700
大手笔啊，奏效了吗？
Quite a thing. Did it work?

590
00:29:41,733 --> 00:29:43,567
-呃，显而易见管用了。
-管用了，哈哈！
-Well, obviously it worked.
-It worked, yeah!

591
00:29:43,600 --> 00:29:45,533
六个月后我就嫁给他了！
I married him
six months later!

592
00:29:45,567 --> 00:29:48,567
-什么？就因为那辆……
-但绝不是因为法拉利！呃……
-What? Because of the...
-But not because of
the Ferrari! Um...

593
00:29:48,600 --> 00:29:51,100
显然也不是因为他的发色，
那肯定……
Not because of the
colour of his hair,
obviously, that's...

594
00:29:51,133 --> 00:29:52,867
-我很喜欢他的发色好吗。
-真的假的？
-I love the colour
of his hair.
-Really?

595
00:29:52,900 --> 00:29:55,267
我超喜欢红发男。
I'm a big fan of the ginge.

596
00:29:55,267 --> 00:29:56,633
-真的？
-真的。
-Really?
-Yeah.

597
00:29:57,367 --> 00:29:59,433
现场有红发的人吗？
Are there any here?

598
00:29:59,467 --> 00:30:01,933
没有，我们不放他们进来。
尽量把他们挡在门外。
No. We don't let them in.
We try to keep them out.

599
00:30:01,967 --> 00:30:05,000
我总觉得他们身上的味儿
不太一样。
They smell different,
I find.

600
00:30:05,033 --> 00:30:08,267
但他当年铺了……
他不是往法拉利上铺满了玫瑰吗？
But he covered it with...
Didn't he cover the Ferrari
with roses?

601
00:30:08,300 --> 00:30:10,267
对，他在车里塞满了玫瑰
Yeah, he filled the car
with roses

602
00:30:10,267 --> 00:30:13,067
而且引擎盖上也全铺满了玫瑰。
and then he covered the bonnet
with roses, too.

603
00:30:13,100 --> 00:30:15,900
-他后来留着那车了吗？
-呃，没有。
-Did he keep it?
-Um, no.

604
00:30:15,933 --> 00:30:18,333
我们把它折价换了
三辆老爷车。
We chopped it in
for three classic cars.

605
00:30:18,367 --> 00:30:19,567
都是些什么车？
Which were?

606
00:30:19,600 --> 00:30:21,033
一辆莫里斯Minor，
Moggy Minor,

607
00:30:21,067 --> 00:30:22,767
一辆捷豹Mark 2……
Jag Mark 2...

608
00:30:23,267 --> 00:30:24,633
-太漂亮了。
-是啊。
-Beautiful.
-Yeah.

609
00:30:24,667 --> 00:30:26,567
还有一辆奔驰，
但我记不清具体是哪款了。
And a Mercedes,
but I can't remember
what it was.

610
00:30:26,600 --> 00:30:27,967
-老款的？
-老款的。
-An old one?
-An old one.

611
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:29,633
-你更喜欢老车？
-对，我超爱老车。
-Do you prefer old cars?
-Yeah, I love old cars.

612
00:30:29,667 --> 00:30:31,167
为什么更喜欢老车？
Why do you like
old cars more?

613
00:30:31,267 --> 00:30:32,833
我觉得它们特别美，
简直就是艺术品。
I just think
they're beautiful,
they're works of art.

614
00:30:32,867 --> 00:30:34,367
我宁可去看老车。
I'd much rather look
at an old car.

615
00:30:34,400 --> 00:30:37,667
我……我对新车真的一点都提不起兴趣。
I have... I'm not a huge fan
of new cars at all.

616
00:30:37,700 --> 00:30:40,500
-那你现在开什么车？
-保时捷911。
-So what's your car now?
-It's a Porsche 911.

617
00:30:40,533 --> 00:30:42,633
天哪！又来一辆911。
Oh God! Not another one.

618
00:30:42,667 --> 00:30:44,700
-1989年的。
-那就是早期的……
-1989.
-So an early...

619
00:30:44,733 --> 00:30:47,100
-这代挺好看的。
-反正就是一辆1989年的
-It's a nice model.
-It's a 1989

620
00:30:47,133 --> 00:30:51,267
保时捷911，给那些
根本懒得管具体底盘代号的人开的。
Porsche 911, for people
who couldn't care less
what model number.

621
00:30:51,267 --> 00:30:53,767
-对，我确实不太懂。
-没错，反正无所谓，不是吗？
-Yeah, I don't really know.
-Yeah, it doesn't really
matter, does it?

622
00:30:53,800 --> 00:30:57,433
我只知道它是白色的，
而且我超喜欢白色的车。
All I know that it's white
and I love white cars.

623
00:30:57,467 --> 00:30:59,933
-哎，这就很有意思了。
-你也喜欢白色的车？
-Now, that's interesting.
-Do you love white cars?

624
00:30:59,967 --> 00:31:01,833
我觉得白色是很有70年代风味的颜色，
I think white's
a good '70s colour

625
00:31:01,867 --> 00:31:04,000
-很快就该卷土重来了。
-没错。
-that should be making
a comeback soon.
-Yeah.

626
00:31:04,033 --> 00:31:05,767
当然了，你是个非常有品位的女人，
You are a woman,
of course, of great taste

627
00:31:05,800 --> 00:31:08,100
因为前几天我还读到一篇报道，
'cause I did find a piece
of writing the other day

628
00:31:08,133 --> 00:31:10,900
-说你喜欢挺着啤酒肚的男人。
-确实喜欢。
-that you like a man
with a beer belly.
-I do.

629
00:31:11,433 --> 00:31:13,167
（比莉大笑）
(BILLIE LAUGHS)

630
00:31:13,267 --> 00:31:14,833
瞧你那得意样。对，我真喜欢。
Smug. Yeah, I do.

631
00:31:14,867 --> 00:31:17,267
但你从不……
六块腹肌那种不是你的菜？
But you never...
The six-pack thing
isn't for you?

632
00:31:17,267 --> 00:31:18,267
完全不是。
It's not for me.

633
00:31:18,267 --> 00:31:20,267
-我一点都不喜欢那种。
-为什么？
-I don't like it at all.
-Why?

634
00:31:20,267 --> 00:31:22,733
太刻意了，用力过猛。
It's just too "try hard".

635
00:31:22,767 --> 00:31:24,467
-就是……你懂的……
-我举双手赞成。
-It's just... You know...
-I agree.

636
00:31:24,500 --> 00:31:26,300
我喜欢的男人得……你懂的……
I like my men... You know...

637
00:31:26,533 --> 00:31:27,933
懂。
Yeah.

638
00:31:27,967 --> 00:31:30,367
我猜你现在觉得自己像个大傻子了吧？
Bet you're feeling like
a bit of berk now, aren't you?

639
00:31:30,400 --> 00:31:32,367
（观众大笑）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

640
00:31:32,400 --> 00:31:34,067
他刚才一直站在那儿摆谱，就男人那种德行
He's been standing there,
you know that thing men do

641
00:31:34,100 --> 00:31:36,133
胳膊还拼命往外
使劲架着？
with they're pushing
the arms out?

642
00:31:36,167 --> 00:31:37,500
瞧瞧他。
Look at him.

643
00:31:37,533 --> 00:31:39,733
“瞧瞧我的大肌肉！
来，瞅瞅这个。”
"Look at my muscles!
Here, look at that."

644
00:31:39,767 --> 00:31:41,467
练得挺不错嘛。
They're very nice.

645
00:31:41,500 --> 00:31:44,267
现在把肚子挺出来。
老兄，你也可以
秀一把了。
Now stick your stomach out.
You might be able to show it,
mate.

646
00:31:44,267 --> 00:31:46,600
话说回来，我想聊聊你的圈速，
在场上跑得感觉如何？
Anyway, I want to talk
about your lap,
how was it out there?

647
00:31:46,633 --> 00:31:49,767
嗯，还行吧。
Um, it was okay.

648
00:31:49,800 --> 00:31:51,767
比我想象中
难多了。
It was a lot harder
than I imagined.

649
00:31:51,800 --> 00:31:54,933
而且我还跑得有点火大，
我觉得这可不太妙。
I got a bit angry as well,
which I don't think's good.

650
00:31:54,967 --> 00:31:56,733
-生斯提格的气？
-生我自己的气。
-Angry with The Stig?
-Myself.

651
00:31:56,767 --> 00:31:58,700
没生斯提格的气。
我超爱斯提格的。
Not with The Stig.
I love The Stig.

652
00:31:58,733 --> 00:32:01,367
-真的吗？
-他特别有耐心，
人特别好。
-Really?
-He's was very patient,
very generous.

653
00:32:01,400 --> 00:32:04,267
-特别……是吗？
-对啊。
-Very... Was he?
-Yeah.

654
00:32:04,267 --> 00:32:06,867
只可惜虽然
他身材练得极好，
It's just unfortunate that
he's got a really toned body.

655
00:32:06,900 --> 00:32:09,167
-有吗？
-是啊，但却长了张
“象人”一样的脸。
-Does he?
-Yeah, and a face like
the Elephant Man.

656
00:32:10,100 --> 00:32:11,300
那可真遗憾。
That's a shame.

657
00:32:11,333 --> 00:32:14,633
-你给……呃，
克里斯打电话请教了……？
-打了。
-Did you call, um,
Chris up to get...
-Yeah.

658
00:32:14,667 --> 00:32:19,767
-他说……
-他说：“听斯提格的，
好好按走线开。”
-And he said...
-He said, "Listen to The Stig
and work with the lines."

659
00:32:19,800 --> 00:32:21,567
想看看回放吗？
Would you like to see it?

660
00:32:21,600 --> 00:32:24,167
-好啊。
-有谁想看
比利的圈速？
-All right.
-Who'd like to
see Billie's lap?

661
00:32:24,267 --> 00:32:26,633
-全场：想！
-好的，咱们来看看。
-ALL: Yeah!
-Okay, let's have a look.

662
00:32:27,300 --> 00:32:28,633
（轮胎尖叫声）
(TYRES SCREECH)

663
00:32:28,667 --> 00:32:29,933
起飞咯！
Shake and bake.

664
00:32:32,067 --> 00:32:33,267
二档。
Second.

665
00:32:34,167 --> 00:32:35,600
杰里米：接着挂三档。
JEREMY: And third next.

666
00:32:35,633 --> 00:32:36,800
哎呀！好吧，你刚才稍微切了点弯，
Oops! Well, you cut the corner
a little bit there

667
00:32:36,833 --> 00:32:38,267
不过嘿，没关系，
but hey, that doesn't matter

668
00:32:38,267 --> 00:32:40,767
因为这只会
拖慢你的速度。
'cause it just slows
you down.

669
00:32:43,533 --> 00:32:45,133
好吧，等等。
All right, wait.

670
00:32:45,167 --> 00:32:47,667
你要往哪开啊？你开到
逆行车道上去了！
Where are you going? You're
on the wrong side of the road!

671
00:32:47,700 --> 00:32:50,700
（毫无波澜地念叨）
一定要干掉戈登·拉姆齐。
(IN MONOTONE)
Must beat Gordon Ramsay.

672
00:32:51,867 --> 00:32:53,433
杰里米：
好的，进入锤头弯，
JEREMY:
Okay, into the Hammerhead

673
00:32:53,467 --> 00:32:58,933
然而，这路线
又彻底走偏了。
and, again, that's entirely
the wrong route.

674
00:32:58,967 --> 00:33:01,267
天呐，太惨不忍睹了。
Oh, God, this is terrible.

675
00:33:01,267 --> 00:33:04,100
杰里米：上一个在这里
迷路迷成这样的，
还是乔纳森·罗斯。
JEREMY: Jonathan Ross
was the last person
here to get this lost.

676
00:33:05,467 --> 00:33:07,933
（哔——）见鬼了。
(BLEEP)...hell.

677
00:33:07,967 --> 00:33:11,400
杰里米：对，走对路了。
没往右边拐，这很棒。
JEREMY: Yeah, got the
right way. Didn't turn
right there. That's good.

678
00:33:11,433 --> 00:33:12,767
